  "root_defect": {
    "observed": "GoW binds 81,882 image descriptors per draw in a pattern where both selected image descriptors have flattened offsets and the sampler is host-uniform. Uniform descriptors are being replaced with nine typed arrays for every table entry.",
    "correction": "Require complete eight-word image and four-word sampler SharpFetch plans with non-Invalid summaries, then retain ordinary binding. GPU-dependent or unresolved descriptors retain indexed tables. Binary shader-cache version 30 to 31; no metadata layout change.",
    "proof_basis": "Flattened offsets are established by the existing host-uniform expression analysis, not by equal sampled values or current validity. RefreshFlatBuf reevaluates live scalar selections and contents; normal specialization retains resource format/view checks.",
    "per_game_changes": false,
    "limits": "This removes demonstrated unnecessary descriptor work. Native FPS gain, visual recovery and universal correctness of the new candidate remain unmeasured."
  },
